;
TEMPORARY WORKSPACE

I0:WORK is caller-readable and writable under the default policy.
It is cleared when a call ends and before the next caller starts.
Do not treat files in WORK as permanent storage.

Game launchers and approved applications can create files in WORK.
There is currently no general caller copy command or direct upload to WORK.
UPLOAD instead submits files privately for sysop review.

The sysop controls access per drive and user area through AUTH.
Caller programs require readable, non-writable storage and file approval.
Consequently programs cannot be executed from caller-writable WORK.
Permission changes and file approval are private sysop operations.
